{"schema_version":1,"observation_id":"events-4b3902bd64e84d569745ce4f87e8b890","run_id":"t1-t7-gpt-5.4-nano-high-t4-swipe-to-seek-linux-run-e019d660bda8","after":25436,"next_sequence":25540,"events":[{"sequence":25437,"timestamp":"2026-08-22T11:08:29.819440Z","elapsed_seconds":1506.81,"source":"pi","event":{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolName":"bash","toolCallId":"call_e1Bi8Sqb3n9miQu74K3CPBvb|fc_0902eeeba234f7f8016a8982fe2de88190a5eff28450196c08","args":{"command":"set -euo pipefail\nLOG=/tmp/nothingness_seek_flutter.log\nrm -f \"$LOG\"\nflutter run -t dev/main_debug.dart -d linux --debug >\"$LOG\" 2>&1 &\nPID=$!\ncleanup(){ kill $PID >/dev/null 2>&1 || true; }\ntrap cleanup EXIT\nBASE=\"\"\nfor i in $(seq 1 240); do\n  if grep -q \"A Dart VM Service\" \"$LOG\"; then\n    BASE=$(grep \"A Dart VM Service\" \"$LOG\" | tail -1 | sed -E 's/.*available at: (http[^ ]+).*/\\1/')\n    [[ \"$BASE\" != */ ]] && BASE=\"$BASE/\"\n    break\n  fi\n  sleep 1\ndone\nif [[ -z \"$BASE\" ]]; then echo \"Failed to find VM service URL\"; tail -n 50 \"$LOG\"; exit 1; fi\nexport BASE\n\necho \"VM_BASE=$BASE\"\n\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport os, json, time, base64, urllib.parse, urllib.request\nbase=os.environ['BASE']\n\ndef ext(name, isolate, params=None):\n    if params is None:\n        params={}\n    q=dict(params)\n    q['isolateId']=isolate\n    url=base+f\"ext.nothingness.{name}?\"+urllib.parse.urlencode(q)\n    with urllib.request.urlopen(url) as resp:\n        data=json.load(resp)\n    if data.get('error'):\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"ext {name} error: {data['error']}\")\n    return data['result']\n\nwith urllib.request.urlopen(base+'getVM') as resp:\n    vm=json.load(resp)\nmain=[i for i in vm['result']['isolates'] if i.get('name')=='main'][0]\nisolate=main['id']\n\nfixtures='/opt/nothingness/media'\ntracks=sorted([f for f in os.listdir(fixtures) if f.endswith('.opus')])\npath=os.path.join(fixtures, tracks[0])\n\next('playTrackByPath', isolate, {'path': path})\n\nfor _ in range(90):\n    st=ext('getPlaybackState', isolate)\n    song=st.get('songInfo')\n    if song and song.get('duration',0)>0:\n        break\n    time.sleep(0.2)\nelse:\n    raise RuntimeError('duration never became available')\n\next('dragByKeyPause', isolate, {\n    'key':'hero-song',\n    'dx':'240',\n    'dy':'0',\n    'steps':'28',\n    'pauseStep':'12',\n    'kind':'touch',\n})\n\ns1=ext('screenshot', isolate, {'pixelRatio':'1.0'})\nopen('/workspace/.tmp/seek_during.png','wb').write(base64.b64decode(s1['png_base64']))\n\next('dragByKeyContinue', isolate, {})\n\ntime.sleep(0.8)\n\ns2=ext('screenshot', isolate, {'pixelRatio':'1.0'})\nopen('/workspace/.tmp/seek_post.png','wb').write(base64.b64decode(s2['png_base64']))\n\nprint('WROTE screenshots')\nPY\n","timeout":1800}}},{"sequence":25438,"timestamp":"2026-08-22T11:08:29.898982Z","elapsed_seconds":1506.89,"source":"pi","event":{"type":"tool_execution_end","toolName":"bash","toolCallId":"call_e1Bi8Sqb3n9miQu74K3CPBvb|fc_0902eeeba234f7f8016a8982fe2de88190a5eff28450196c08","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"VM_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:35379/FFAB07XF8NY=/\nWROTE screenshots\n"}]},"isError":false}},{"sequence":25439,"timestamp":"2026-08-22T11:08:30.041577Z","elapsed_seconds":1507.032,"source":"pi","event":{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_e1Bi8Sqb3n9miQu74K3CPBvb|fc_0902eeeba234f7f8016a8982fe2de88190a5eff28450196c08","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VM_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:35379/FFAB07XF8NY=/\nWROTE screenshots\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787396909896}}},{"sequence":25440,"timestamp":"2026-08-22T11:08:30.097969Z","elapsed_seconds":1507.089,"source":"pi","event":{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_e1Bi8Sqb3n9miQu74K3CPBvb|fc_0902eeeba234f7f8016a8982fe2de88190a5eff28450196c08","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VM_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:35379/FFAB07XF8NY=/\nWROTE screenshots\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787396909896}}},{"sequence":25441,"timestamp":"2026-08-22T11:08:30.257144Z","elapsed_seconds":1507.248,"source":"pi","event":{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Considering pointer events**\n\nI\u2019m thinking that maybe it\u2019d be simpler not to use PointerAddedEvent at all. In dragByKey, they trigger pointerAdded and removed events for real touch simulation. But for dragByKeyPause, could we mimic dragByKey\u2019s behavior with a pointerRemoved event at the end? If so, that might release the drag. Alternatively, maybe we can send a PointerAddedEvent, followed by PointerDown and PointerRemoved. But I\u2019m not sure if that would keep the gesture active, since pointerRemoved may cancel the gesture. Using 'touch' instead of 'mouse' might help avoid the MouseTracker issue referenced in the stack trace.\n\n**Adjusting pointer kind settings**\n\nI think I\u2019ll adjust by using `kind='touch'` in the dragByKeyPause call. This will set PointerDeviceKind to touch, which, importantly, avoids using the mouse tracker! I\u2019ll also update the automation script to set kind as 'touch' instead of 'mouse'. Even so, the GestureDetector might behave differently. So, the simplest approach is to invoke dragByKeyPause with kind touch and see if that resolves the assertion issue. Additionally, for the screenshot, we\u2019ll stick with kind touch to avoid problems. Finally, I\u2019ll rerun the automation to ensure everything works smoothly.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0902eeeba234f7f8016a8982ec32908190986062420a1d2daa\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqiYL-f4gkXMh016pjxfDgdjwDC93ffjAyXl-LL0hPjrk0U-dUaY-s0OQb-kTcYtTQPoZ-g5acimMokwONv5EXa-gTSI_beuTPAefTbW4KZV6y-xvxW9Ffd-BGu9YiWFLxCcvDIk8gcUOUHfg9IKJ_cvK8T3f0LFamV1MfnZvYkmRusOMpsKueLTvib6dWclIBNdBR_Loc80Yi86iPEeB8K4UfFG3vknrUIyb4oMLhsyBvxTRuJkHftKUMRSpfCBGAOOkpBabsbCo6TYgoPrNaVBcPxInxyR6xDPurTOYbmSTArctqOtjRB-DT-Iz80G1eqlCQ9y0